    "notes": [
      "Photo-1 (columns 1–2, row 7) has no '1' marker while photo-2 and photo-3 carry '2' and '3'. Add the same boxed numeral in its lower-left corner so the three steps read as one numbered sequence.",
      "The steps grow unevenly in height: photo-1 is 1 row, photo-2 is 2 rows, photo-3 is 5 rows. The 2-to-5 jump breaks the rhythm. Either make the heights 1, 2, 4 rows and end photo-3 at row 10, or make them 1, 3, 5 rows so each step adds two rows.",
      "Photo-3's crop does not deliver the idea that 'the front door fills the frame'. The arch sits only in the bottom third of columns 7–12, and the bay window dominates. Re-crop so the doorway fills rows 8–11, with the arch top near row 8.",
      "Rows 9–10 hold the lead, but its third line ends early in row 10, leaving a dead strip above the body in row 11. Either start the body at row 10 with one empty baseline after the lead, or keep it in row 11 and add a short rule or numeral so the gap reads as intended.",
      "The body bottom (row 12) overshoots photo-3's bottom edge (row 11). Align the body so its last baseline sits on the row-11 bottom line, level with photo-3. Then the caption in row 12 stands alone as the closing element of columns 7–12.",
      "Photo-1 is so small at 2 columns that it reads as a thumbnail, not as step one of a zoom. Consider starting it at 3 columns (1–3), with photo-2 at 4 columns (4–7) and photo-3 at 5 columns (8–12), so the steps scale visibly.",
      "The body rag breaks 'Mavis / Lever' across lines 4–5. Rebreak by widening the body to the full 6 columns (1–6), matching the lead's span, or tighten the tracking so the name stays on one line.",
      "The red is used only once, in the step-label at column 7, row 6. Repeat it on the three photo numerals so the accent connects the label to the sequence it describes."
    ],
    "summary": "A clear, worthwhile idea with a strong 12-column headline and a sensible left and right split. The zoom sequence is under-built, though. Photo-1 is unnumbered and too small, the row steps grow unevenly (1, 2, 5), and photo-3 does not actually end on the door. Tighten the step proportions, align the body and photo-3 bottoms on row 11, and carry the red into the numerals.",
    "mean": 6.8
  },
